            "toc_label": "Chlorine",
            "anchor": "chlorine",
            "text": "<p>US water utilities add chlorine or chloramine to treat tap water. In a hot shower, that chlorine meets warm skin, your scalp and steam, and it strips the natural oils that keep skin and hair comfortable.</p><p>If your skin feels tight after showering, or your hair feels rough when it dries, chlorine is a likely part of it.</p>"
